    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "terrainName": "farm",
    "description": "What: a farm under fire (CE-4623 AB-10, docs/designs/animals/DESIGN_Animals.md \u00a76.2). Five ANIMAL AREAS populate at the start: 'Pasture' (8 cattle, by the lane), 'Farm dog' at the farmhouse, 'Hens', 'Pig pen' (3 pigs, enclosed) and 'Orchard birds' (one flock of 30 in the orchard). An 'M1 Abrams' drives the lane east and turns up the track into the pasture's south edge, then away. At 40 s a 'Rifleman' north-west of the orchard fires 20 rounds at a berm. Judge: (1) the tank frightens the herd: cows panic and flee (2) the herd runs away from the tank, north, and at least one cow breaks through the wooden fence (beyond y = 64) (3) the birds stay perched (and singing) until the shots (4) the shots flush the flock (it flies) and the birdsong stops (the flock is frightened) (5) the pigs stay in their pen. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh farm-under-fire"
  },
